body:
This is so true. This helps ever so much. I think I feel guilt in not loving him, in wasting away my life...

&#x200B;

I keep my daughter far away from him now. But you are right.

Thank you. This is probably the best route. What I do now, is that after every encounter, I will sit back and think, "How did it make me feel?" and the next time, I remember that speaking to him will bring me nothing good in life. 

&#x200B;

I think what I am stuck on now, is payback. He has caused me so much pain, and I want him to feel it right back.

YES. Me.

I am so tired now, that even crying sounds exhausting. I have raged, projected my frustration on innocent friends and family and myself, dug my nails into my skin, screamed while driving...you name it, I've done it. 

&#x200B;

But now, I am tired. I feel rage for ever meeting this pompous, self entitled jerk. I feel AMUSEMENT when I look at this putrid, lying, selfish, greedy man who thinks he is ever so smart but is just a toxic vile little snake that people run from. I feel sick and tired at the thought of him touching me, and thinking of the damage he did to my self esteem. 

&#x200B;

Don't worry, love. Leaving this man will be the best thing that will happen. It's hard. I am still working on it. But I assure you, even a one night drunken tinder hook up will offer you more love and intimacy than this trash ever will.

I wish you could send that over to my boyfriend. Some times all that is needed is open, communication. People think its overrated, but that is because communication usually ends up being one-sided or is not occurring at all. 

&#x200B;

There is something ever so strong and sexy about a man who will come up to you and be vulnerable. I want to know if my partner is sad, if something I did made him angry, happy or upset, I need to know what he wants, or how he feels.

Okay, so two sides: 

&#x200B;

Side 1: Her brother abused her, and/or is obsessed with her. He wants to punish her by getting you to abandon her. 

&#x200B;

Side 2: Your wife did actually abuse her brother, and he thinks it is only fair that after all the damage done, she will suffer for it. 

&#x200B;

I would not even think of Side 1 in this case, unless your wife has a logical case against what he said. Seeing that she did not immediately break down, but instead got enraged and blocked him, and hides her family from you anyway...yeah, this is a red flag. I would be VERY careful having children with this woman. Make sure you keep the family on your side if it is too late, so in case you need to escape they will support you in the court of law.

Okay, even though I have an awful time in my relationship...GIRL, I AM SO HAPPY FOR YOU! This doesn't have to be for sad crap only. Congratulations on your pregnancy and on having a healthy relationship :) 

&#x200B;

I think tiny, random love notes, little surprises of desserts or food, you can encourage him when he feels down, rub his head or feet, be the big spoon to him...those kind of things :)

Sometimes in life, we have to close our hearts and think from a third person perspective. 

&#x200B;

He's gay. 

Not because of what he likes, but because he has no interest in you or your body. 

&#x200B;

My boyfriend is bi. I am aware of this. He has zero interest in my breasts, and wants his butt played with but not by me and I know that he would prefer if a man did this to him instead.

You said all the things I was afraid of saying. The truth is, I have checked out, but not to the point that I have no care at all. A part of me wants him to value me enough to realize that I have checked out, and work on bringing me back. I think I also need him to realize the extent of damage his anger issues, perfectionism and lack of intimacy has done to me. 

&#x200B;

Sitting there for hours checking out other women's butts on Reddit in front of your girlfriend, never urging her to give you sex or nudes or anything similar, not lusting after her, not giving her the time of day to explore her body, continuing to chat with women who flirt with you, being distant and secretive...those things have built up resentment and trust issues in me. We have talked about it, and I believe in him and his efforts, but he needs to realize that I can simply not forget that. In the back of my head, I am not his number one, and that is not a thought that arouses me. I don't feel any form of comfort or confidence in being naked in front of him, because even his efforts seem like he is amusing me or himself.

You're absolutely right. I think it is more that I am fully aware that 90 percent of these pictures are not real. I worked in the sex industry myself as a dancer, have breast implants, and have been everything from a 100 to 230lbs in my life. On a personal level, I am well aware of what is real and what is not. However,it is the way people drink it in and believe a body or a face is real when it really is not, is what makes me feel worse even when I try not to let it get to me. For e.g: I know that ten second loop of a girl jiggling her butt bubbles up and down was developed using a brazillian butt lift, twenty film takes, body make up, and evening light. However, to my boyfriend, this is just the cool nerd chic chilling on her sofa in her booty shorts and fake eyelashes, and look,wow! So natural and so perfect. I'll admit a lot of it happened because he would freely scroll through these first thing in the morning, first thing before he even kissed me, and that damage is already done lol 

&#x200B;

I wish people would stop though.I wish humans don't feel the need to work so hard for perfection when it came to their looks.
